PN,36402
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F364A1785349119
OL,3,CArson suspect found dead in bin days
OL,4,Cafter fatal house fire
OL,6,FA hearing in Liverpool, on 29 July,
OL,7,Fwas told that Smith's body was
OL,8,Fdiscovered in a wheelie bin seven days
OL,9,Fafter the fatal fire, having taken a
OL,10,Flethal cocktail of drugs.
OL,12,FPolice were first alerted on 22 July
OL,13,F2025 after receiving a call from a man
OL,14,Fnamed Steven Wales.
OL,16,FHe informed officers that a man had
OL,17,Feither drowned or suffered a fatal
OL,18,Foverdose in the bath of a property on
OL,19,FConiston Street, Everton, two days
OL,20,Fprior to the call.
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G2/7
OL,2,W/*%+.-' "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNW Eng NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,365,360,120,260,000,100
PN,36403
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F364A1785349119
OL,3,CArson suspect found dead in bin days
OL,4,Cafter fatal house fire
OL,6,FSenior coroner for Liverpool Andre
OL,7,FRebello said: "Merseyside Police were
OL,8,Fdeployed and located a male, deceased,
OL,9,Fin a wheelie bin at the rear of
OL,10,Fderelict properties on Thirlmere Road,
OL,11,Fwhich backs on to Coniston Street and
OL,12,Fis separated by an alleyway.
OL,14,F"The deceased male was identified by
OL,15,Fpolice as Paul Joseph Smith."
OL,17,FSmith, 40, who lived on Lower Breck
OL,18,FRoad, had last spoken to his family on
OL,19,F19 July and was reported missing by
OL,20,Fhis brother on 21 July.
OL,26,@oD@OOUvD@AOUwD@]O]
OL,1,W~k4j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G3/7
